    "explanation": "Rider and driver, here is the decision.\n\nWhat the record shows. The trip was accepted at 07:09:15 on 28 Aug 2026. The driver tapped 'I'm Here' at 07:18:21 and the app's 180-second free waiting timer started at 07:18:23 (EV-TRIP-02726). The GPS trace (EV-GPS-02726: 100% coverage, 88 fixes, no gaps, weight 1.0) puts the driver's first qualifying fix inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius at 07:20:21, and shows one continuous qualifying run of 150 seconds made of 16 fixes, ending at 07:22:51. The driver cancelled at 07:22:54 with the code RIDER_NO_SHOW.\n\nWhy the fee comes back. POL-NS-01(c) measures the required wait from the driver's first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix, not from the 'arrived' tap. On that measure the driver waited 150 seconds against the 180 seconds in force for this trip (EV-TRIP-02726 platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180) — a shortfall of 30 seconds. POL-NS-06 makes that shortfall a refund in full whether or not the rider was present and whether or not she responded to messages. No driver compensation is payable: POL-NS-07 pays only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and limb (c) is not, because the effective dwell fell short.\n\nThe amount. SGD 4.50 — the cancellation-fee line on the ledger (EV-FARE-02726: cancellation_fee 4.50, total_charged 4.50, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00), which is also the amount contested.\n\nThe rider's claim that the driver was still far away on the main road when the app said he had arrived, and the driver's own statement 'I pressed arrived a bit early but I did wait at the pin', point the same way, and the trace agrees: the tap preceded the driver's first in-geofence fix by 120 seconds (EV-GPS-02726 dwell_start_offset_sec = -120). The refund does not depend on whether the tap qualifies as a false arrival marker under POL-NS-05, because the waiting clock is measured from the geofence entry in any event; the 30-second shortfall decides the case. One claim on the driver's side is not sound and I do not rely on it: the driver's mean distance across the whole trace (about 3.1 km, maximum 8.1 km) does not fix his position at the moment of the tap, and a mean over the whole journey cannot do that — but nothing turns on it.\n\nOn the rider-contact point, both sides agree and I confirm: the rider's own track (EV-GPS-02726) shows 60 fixes all about 736 m from the pin, outside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius, so POL-NS-04 limb (c) is failed and that clause does not exonerate the rider. Under POL-NS-11 that makes no difference to this refund, which rests on the driver's own arrival and dwell evidence; the rider's evidence is not the carrier of any deciding fact here.\n\nEscalation and referrals checked; none is engaged. The driver's profile shows 2 no-show terminations in the trailing 30 days against 94 completed trips (a rate of about 0.021), so the POL-NS-07 anti-farming test does not trip (it needs 4 or more AND a rate above 0.08), and POL-NS-09(d) does not fire; neither profile shows any dispute with the other party in the trailing 90 days, so POL-NS-09(c) does not fire. The GPS trace carries no gap over 120 seconds and 88 fixes, so it is not impaired under POL-NS-08(a) to (d) and POL-NS-09(e) does not apply. No clause produces a referral on these facts: POL-NS-05's false-arrival referral arises only where the trace contains no qualifying in-geofence fix anywhere (there are 16) or where the corrected dwell still meets the minimum (it does not), and POL-NS-07's escalation packet is not reached because compensation is simply not payable.\n\nConfidence and execution. The deciding fact — a 150-second in-geofence dwell against a 180-second minimum — is carried by EV-GPS-02726 and EV-TRIP-02726, both at weight_multiplier 1.0, so my confidence is capped at 1.0 under POL-GEN-02(2); I have set it at 0.9, above the 0.70 floor. The monetary effect, SGD 4.50, is below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00, so this refund executes on issue; the charge to the rider is reversed. For disclosure: two claims raised in the debate were discarded by the citation referee before I saw them, both because they cited the missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02726-01 (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) without naming that issue code as POL-GEN-02(1) requires; they did not bear on the outcome. The absence of that advisory also means POL-NS-06(i) cannot be used to add separate in-geofence intervals together, but the trace shows a single interval (run_count 1) in any event, so the 150-second figure stands. This is a provisional ruling; either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04 within 30 days."
