    "explanation": "To the rider and to the driver: the record supports both accounts, and the outcome is a full refund of the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee.\n\nWhat happened. The trip record (EV-TRIP-02726) shows the driver tapped 'I'm Here' at 07:18:21 and the platform started a 180-second free waiting period at 07:18:23; the driver cancelled at 07:22:54 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-02726) shows the driver's first qualifying fix inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius at 07:20:21 — 120 seconds after the tap (dwell_start_offset_sec -120) — and one continuous qualifying run of 150 seconds, 07:20:21 to 07:22:51, on 16 qualifying fixes. The free waiting period in force is 180 seconds (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180). Effective dwell 150 s against 180 s required leaves a 30-second shortfall.\n\nWhy the fee does not stand. POL-NS-01 charges the fee only if all four limbs hold. Limb (a) holds (the record carries an 'arrived' event). Limb (b) holds on the recomputed clock. Limb (c) fails: POL-NS-01(c) measures the dwell from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix, not from the arrival tap, and that dwell is 150 seconds against the 180 required. Limb (d) fails too, because the required dwell had not elapsed when the driver cancelled. The fee is therefore not chargeable under POL-NS-01, and the refund follows from POL-NS-05 and POL-NS-06. POL-NS-10 does not apply: the cancellation was the driver's, not the rider's; and POL-NS-03 does not apply, because the driver's stationary fixes are inside the arrival radius, essentially at the pin (minimum distance 0.35 m).\n\nThe false marker and the shortfall. Both advocates argued, and I accept, that the 07:18:21 arrival tap does not start the waiting clock: it preceded the first qualifying in-geofence fix by 120 seconds. On the recomputed basis the corrected dwell (150 s) is shorter than the free waiting period, so POL-NS-05(i) refunds the fee in full with no driver compensation. Independently, POL-NS-06 makes the same shortfall a strict-liability refund, whether or not the rider was present and whether or not the rider responded to messages. Even setting the marker question aside, POL-NS-01(c) measures the dwell from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, so the 30-second shortfall decides the case either way.\n\nThe driver's statement. The driver's own statement, 'I pressed arrived a bit early but I did wait at the pin', is accepted: it is an admission against his own interest and it corroborates the trace-derived finding that the tap preceded his actual in-geofence presence.\n\nThe rider's position. The rider track places the rider's device about 740 m from the pin (mean 739.6 m, minimum 735.9 m) across 60 fixes, all at 0.0 kph, outside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius, and rider_qualifying_fix_count is 0. POL-NS-04 limb (c) is therefore affirmatively failed and that clause does not exonerate the rider; POL-NS-11 does not apply because the test can be run. This does not change the refund: POL-NS-06 returns the fee regardless of rider presence, and the refund rests on the driver's own arrival and dwell evidence, not on rider contact.\n\nThe trace-wide distance figures. The claim that the driver was 'still far away on the main road' is accepted in substance — he was not at the pin when he tapped. I do not base anything on the trace-wide aggregates (mean distance 3101 m, maximum 8067 m, speeds 30.5–46.9 kph): those are averages and extremes across the whole trace, including the approach, and do not fix his position at the tap. The decisive numbers are the 120-second offset and the 150-second qualifying run.\n\nDriver compensation. It is nil. POL-NS-07 pays the driver only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full; limb (c) fails and POL-NS-06 displaces the fee. The anti-farming check is not reached, and in any event it would not trip (no_show_terminations_30d = 2, below the 4 required, and 2/94 = 0.021, below 0.08). No profile field other than the two POL-NS-07 names was used for that check.\n\nThe money. EV-FARE-02726 shows cancellation_fee 4.50 and total_charged 4.50, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00, and the line reconciles with the net figure produced by the resolution rule. The contested amount is live and is refunded in full: SGD 4.50, the cancellation-fee line only; no booking or platform fee was charged on this cancelled trip. The monetary effect (SGD 4.50) is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold of POL-GEN-05, so it executes automatically on issue, subject to the appeal route in POL-GEN-04.\n\nNo escalation and no referral. Nothing in POL-NS-09 fires: confidence is above the 0.70 floor; the difference between the arrival tap and the trace is a false-marker question that POL-NS-05 resolves, not an unresolved contradiction; neither profile shows a no-show dispute between this rider and this driver (both 0); the anti-farming check does not trip and rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0; and no artifact is impaired under POL-NS-08(a)–(d) (the trace has 100% coverage, no gap over 120 s, the chat sequence is intact and its count matches chat_message_count = 1, and the fare line reconciles). No referral is produced either: POL-NS-05(ii) fires only where no qualifying in-geofence fix exists anywhere in the trip, and one does; POL-NS-05(iii) fires only where the corrected dwell still meets the minimum, and it does not.\n\nA note on the traffic advisory. EV-ADVIS-02726-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0), so POL-NS-06(i) accumulation is unavailable and the single 150-second run (run_count 1) is the operative figure. Two claims resting on that artifact were discarded at the mechanical check for not disclosing its MISSING_ARTIFACT impairment; they were not needed, because the shortfall is established from the trace and the trip record alone."
